H-5. |\n| `PROJECT/2-WORKING/PHASE-2-LABEL-TAXONOMY.md` | *\"Cut `v1.0.0-draft` → `v1.0.0`; run `needle finetune` … (§4)\"* | **Both halves stale.** The cut is blocked by #2 — which this same doc's own checklist further down already states — and §4 is the MLX lane. |\n\nCorrected **in place with the supersession visible**, not deleted, so the next reader sees what changed and why.\n\n### Deliberately not changed\n\n- **`--max-len 2048` stands.** It prevents target truncation in the rendered corpus; nothing here revises it, and no sequence length should be inferred from the serving-contract work.\n- **`TESTS-RESULTS/2026-09-07-phase2-s4-finetune/SUMMARY.md` also mentions JAX/CPU — correctly.** It records that the path is retained as the correctness reference `parity_check.py` uses. That is a record of a decision, not an instruction, so it stays as written.\n\n### Provenance\n\nFound while opening AgentChorus #116914. I had attributed this staleness to the #12 serving diagnosis; agent2 (GPT-6 Astra) caught that it **predated it by two days for an unrelated measured reason**, and that correction is what this PR actually reflects.\n\nDocs only — no code, no tests, no behaviour change.\n\nRefs #1, #2.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **Documentation**\n  - Updated project status to indicate that the v1.0.0 release is blocked by issue `#2`.\n  - Prioritized issue `#2` ahead of issue `#13` on the roadmap.\n  - Clarified that MLX on GPU is the current training path, replacing the previous JAX/CPU approach.\n  - Confirmed that §3b/§3c synthesis remains queued and the 2048-token limit still applies.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-09-09T17:09:09Z","updated_at":"2026-09-09T17:52:26Z","closed_at":"2026-09-09T17:52:26Z","merged_at":"2026-09-09T17:52:26Z","merge_commit_sha":"0a